course: dictionary
lesson: 11934
title: Cancelled: stopped, or made simpler
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cancelled is a word with more than one meaning. Most often it means called off, so a planned thing will not happen. «The football match was cancelled because of the snow.» The match did not take place, because the snow stopped it. Look at the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
explain: Cancelled can also mean no longer valid. «Her train ticket was cancelled, so she could not get on the train.» The ticket still exists, but it no longer works. If the word is near a ticket, an order or a card, it probably means no longer valid.
explain: In maths, cancelled means simplified. «Cancel the fraction 6/8 down to 3/4.» You divide the top and the bottom by the same number, here 2. The fraction keeps the same value but is written more simply. Try the word "stopped" in the sentence: it does not make sense, so this is the maths meaning.
fact: Cancelled means stopped or called off, so a planned thing will not happen.
fact: «Cancelled» can also mean no longer valid, like a cancelled ticket or order.
fact: In maths, «cancelled» means simplified: 6/8 cancelled down becomes 3/4 when you divide both numbers by 2.
fact: Useful phrases: cancelled due to, cancelled because of, cancelled out, and cancel down a fraction.
fact: UK spelling is «cancelled» and «cancelling»; US spelling is often «canceled» and «canceling».
exercise: «The school trip was cancelled because of the storm.» What does cancelled mean here? | *Called off, so it did not happen | Painted bright red | Made simpler | Finished early
exercise: «Her cancelled ticket could not be used.» What does cancelled mean here? | Sold for less money | Simplified, like a fraction | *No longer valid, so it cannot be used | Shouted loudly
exercise: In maths, 6/8 is cancelled down to 3/4. What number do you divide the top and the bottom by? | 8 | *2 | 1 | 4
test: «The concert was cancelled due to illness.» What does the phrase «due to illness» tell you? | The date of the concert | *The reason the concert was called off | The name of the singer | The price of the tickets
test: To cancel the fraction 9/12 down, what do you do? | *Divide the top and the bottom by 3 | Take 3 away from the top only | Add 9 and 12 | Multiply both numbers by 4
exam: Which sentence uses cancelled to mean simplified? | «My order was cancelled by the shop.» | «The ticket was cancelled at the desk.» | *«Cancel 10/15 down to 2/3 by dividing by 5.» | «The picnic was cancelled.»
